## Summary
Workers and citizens staged a sit-in at Sejong Hotel to demand reinstatement, leading to 16 individuals being referred to prosecutors. The protest highlights labor rights issues and the legal consequences for civil disobedience in South Korea.

## Key Points
- Protest occurred at Sejong Hotel lobby with demands for reinstatement of workers.
- 16 participants were collectively referred to prosecutors.
- The event underscores ongoing labor disputes and activism in South Korea.
- Legal action taken against protesters indicates strict enforcement of laws on civil disobedience.


